00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.749 align:start position:0%
homeless and in desperate need of help  36 villages in eastern sudan have been  inundated by water  and the threat from floods isn't over  yet  the torrential rains began more than  five weeks ago el gash a seasonal river  near the city of casella has reached  unprecedented levels and threatens to  spill into surrounding areas  flooding is our biggest problem we've  been asking for a bridge to be built in  this area since 2017  but authorities never responded to our  demands  local authorities say several people  have lost their lives in this area so  far fifteen thousand homes have been  completely or partly damaged  slaves of agricultural land have been  destroyed thousands of families have  lost their livelihoods  it continues to rain and people have  lost their homes now they need shelters  mosquito nets insecticides  castle authorities are appealing for  humanitarian help  the people who have been affected were  already among the poorest in this area  so we would like to ask good hearted  people and organizations to intervene  and bring more help  several countries including qatar and  saudi arabia have already responded  large shipments of aid have been sent by  air and are being distributed but  logistics issues are delaying the  operation many of the affected areas are  remote and have been impossible to reach  because the roads have been cut off by  floods  14 states across sudan need immediate  help  the deadly floods have caused extensive  damage to property especially in the  states of cordovan darfur al jazeera and  white nile  with a few more weeks of the wet season  remaining  fears are mounting but the situation for  those already affected might go from bad  to worse muhammad al-jazeera cartoon
 

